// A built-in role can never be deleted, even by a project's own role
// manager. The source schema's own validation proves this directly:
// `role:admin#delete: []` (empty — no one can satisfy it) versus
// `role:project_manager#delete` (non-empty — a non-built-in role CAN be
// deleted by the same admin). Formalized: pin p as manageable (m is a
// role_manager of p), pin r as p's own role AND flagged built_in_role —
// ask whether delete(m, r) is still reachable despite that. Exclusion
// (`project->role_manager - built_in_role->role_manager`) should block
// it structurally, the same way org#view's exclusion already does in
// schema/example.invariant — expected: exact monotone HOLDS.
invariant built_in_role_never_deletable {
  m: user
  p: project
  r: role

  project(r) = p
  built_in_role(r) = p

  goal: delete(m, r)
}
